SUMMARY:Author Talk: David Kruh - ﻿Little Mister Victory
LOCATION:East Boston Library\, 365 Bremen St\, East Boston\, MA 02128
DESCRIPTION:On August 15\, 1945\, as Bostonians celebrated the end of World
  War II\, a well-dressed woman asked a teenage boy to watch her newborn ba
 by. She promised to return after performing an errand but never did. Littl
 e Mister Victory: A Daughter's Search for the Woman Who Abandoned Her Fath
 er on VJ Day is the true story of a lifelong quest\, by the baby's daughte
 r\, to find the woman who abandoned her father.\nhttps://bpl.bibliocommons
 .com/events/6ab17e446074830038288a76\nFrom Pushpin Boston: https://pushpin
 .city/boston/
URL:https://bpl.bibliocommons.com/events/6ab17e446074830038288a76
END:VEVENT
